Z||000000||turbo86se||09-11-2001||11:55 AM||||Hi everyone, last night I started removing the interior of my 86SE to clean it up, and to find out what those two toggle switches are for. Turned out they were wired, but the wires went no where! <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/eek.gif"><BR>While I've got the interior apart, I'd like to add the optional lights to my SE. I'm talking about the lights that are by the fuse box and passenger footrest. I've got the wire from a '84SE, but I don't know where to hook it up to near the fuse box.<P>I'd also like to hook up the trunk light, my Fiero doesn't. What do I need to do this?<P>Oh yeah, all three of my Fieros have the front compartment light, but they don't work. Do I need to do something special? Or am I missing something?<P>Six days and counting...no more WEBTV!!! ||||reg||1
Z||000001||Indiana_resto_guy||09-11-2001||12:21 PM||||There should be a plug by the power distribution box on the left side foot well above and to the left of fuse box.<BR>I haven't figured out the front compartment light as yet myself!<BR>Someone said (I think) that it comes on with the parking lights and the lid open? Mine (any of them) don't work.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Jncomutt||09-11-2001||12:46 PM||||My front compartment light only comes on with the parking lights on.  I don't know why is wasn't wired to come on when its opended...  maybe so it didn't get stuck on and drain power???||||reg||1
Z||000003||Carrolles||09-12-2001||07:47 AM||||The under dash lights need to be wired into the orange and white wires for interior lights (if I recall correctly).<P>Try this for help<BR> <A HREF="http://home.t-online.de/home/u.moeller-objects/schaltp.html" TARGET=_blank>http://home.t-online.de/home/u.moeller-objects/schaltp.html</A> ||||reg||1
